``\r\nGLM: version 0.9.8.3\r\nGLM: Clang compiler detected\r\nGLM: 64 bits model\r\nGLM: AVX instruction set\r\nGLM: C++11\r\nGLM: Swizzling operators disabled, #define GLM_SWIZZLE to enable swizzle operators\r\nGLM: Depth clip space: negative one to one\r\nGLM: Coordinate system: right handed\r\nGLM: .length() returns glm::length_t, a typedef of int following the GLSL specification\r\n```\r\nHere the errors:\r\n```\r\nIn file included from /usr/local/include/glm/glm.hpp:88:\r\nIn file included from /usr/local/include/glm/integer.hpp:6:\r\nIn file included from /usr/local/include/glm/detail/func_integer.hpp:203:\r\nIn file included from /usr/local/include/glm/detail/func_integer.inl:366:\r\n/usr/local/include/glm/detail/func_integer_simd.inl:54:10: error: use of undeclared identifier '_mm_popcnt_u32'\r\n                return _mm_popcnt_u32(x);\r\n                       ^\r\n/usr/local/include/glm/detail/func_integer_simd.inl:61:27: error: use of undeclared identifier '_mm_popcnt_u64'\r\n                return static_cast<int>(_mm_popcnt_u64(x));\r\n                                        ^\r\n```\r\nIn RELEASE mode no errors are emitted.\r\nAs expected when using #define GLM_FORCE_SSE42, no errors are emitted, even in DEBUG mode. But opposed to the issue header; disabling inlining by not using `GLM_FORCE_INLINE` resulted in the same errors in debug mode as with inlining.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/262496263/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"visorz","id":1767472,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njc0NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1767472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/visorz","html_url":"https://github.com/visorz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/visorz/followers","following_url":"https://